  "response_text": "If the PSP is not set to point to the thread\u2019s stack before trying to run the thread, the processor will try to use an uninitialized or invalid stack pointer or return from the system call. When the runFirstThread() function is called, the processor expects a valid, correctly ordered stack at the PSP location. If PSP is not set, the CPU will ultimately and hard fault by performing an illegal operation. Setting PSP ensures that the processor has a valid stack to pop the simulated thread context from.\\n",
